Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Default hold-Space native2x/release1x locally qualified; publication pending.
Dependencies: Completed workstream24 and existing source-counted keyboard input.

Purpose
-------
Make Space a default momentary native fast-forward shortcut, not a speed toggle.

Tasks
-----
[x] Verify actual pinned EmulatorJS4.2.3 hold/ratio/toggle support.
[x] Route Space through existing host/child keyboard and checked input bridge.
[x] Apply native2x while held and explicitly return1x on release.
[x] Release on blur, hidden page, mode/settings/fullscreen changes.
[x] Prevent repeat keydown from re-engaging after a cancelled hold.
[x] Keep dock feedback, native VSync pacing and settings snapshots consistent.
[x] Preserve explicit GBA Space remaps and do not persist a transient held speed.
[x] Complete final focused native-clock/lifecycle/compatibility qualification.
[ ] Publish through the normal complete gate and independently verify live behavior.
[x] Update affected help/guide/architecture and causal records.

Acceptance criteria
-------------------
Default Space hold measurably accelerates an original native cartridge to2x;
keyup restores1x, including after a prior latched3x/4x choice. Repeat, modal,
blur and mode transitions cannot leave or restart a stuck boost. The native
runtime is retained; form Space behavior/custom GBA bindings remain intact.
Speed is actual core pacing, not a requestAnimationFrame or screenshot trick.

Completion evidence
-------------------
Read exact CDN4.2.3GameManager.js: lines25-26 wrap native fast-forward
toggle/ratio; simulateInput index27 is momentary but inverts latched state.
Read emulator.js4264-4280: native setting changes invoke those functions.
Use that existing setting path and VSync coordination, not raw27inversion.
Both bindKeyboard callers add fastForward:Space after existing GBA mappings.
Native source sets aggregate holds; host speed acknowledgements update dock.
withFastForward changes in-memory speed options, not held-speed localStorage.
Settings release before snapshot; configure cancels stale held speed.
Unit regression covers repeat/blur/cleanup. Syntax/build/all12units pass.
Initial new native browser case reaches its final hidden-iframe focus assertion
after clock/storage/3x/menu/blur/fullscreen checks pass; canvas was not keyboard
focusable. Explicitly make the test fixture canvas focusable and assert actual
focus. The unchanged product passes focused native case18.3s.
Existing full native speed-clock and quick-actions cases pass22.7s/40.0s.
Final expanded native-clock/lifecycle/custom-Space case and existing speed-clock/
quick-actions group pass3/3 in1.4m. Actual cartridge clock measures59.956fps
baseline,119.379fps held and59.638fps released. Inspect, explicit GBA Space
priority, host/child/fullscreen/menu and repeat-after-blur coverage pass.
Final static build passes. Publication qualification remains pending.

